Connect and send be-java's std/net requests on the common pool, never in the async step that calls stdNetSend.
Upstream: not yet; to offer Kotlin Temper with patch 0008.

Kotlin's opened the connection and wrote the body in the caller,
blocking a turn; now all of it runs on the pool, which completes the
future, queueing its waiter. A refused connection still breaks the
promise.

